  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001, multimodal/multiprofile/scgpt/imagenet_vit_l/transformer/concat) achieved 50.7% accuracy, which is moderate and does not yet tell us whether the image modality is contributing positively or negatively. The most fundamental uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion is actually beneficial over RNA-only modeling. config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, transformer) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_001—only the image modality is removed while all other settings (profile, RNA encoder, aggregation) remain identical. If rna_only matches or exceeds 50.7%, it signals that the image branch is not adding value and I should redirect the remaining 8 experiments toward RNA-encoder and aggregation choices. If it falls well below, the multimodal direction is validated and I can exploit it by varying encoders and fusion. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the highest-leverage design axis before committing the remaining budget."
}

